{"term":"bureaucracy","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d59a43333bdfceada3","definition":"Government by bureaus or their administrators or officers.","example":"However, when Britain left the European Union, ferries started to ply a direct sea link from Ireland, to save hauliers from custom's bureaucracy of driving via Britain.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["antibureaucracy","bureaucrap","bureaucrat","bureaucratese","bureaucratic","bureaucratically","bureaucratize","bureaucrazy","bureaupathology","Eurocracy","technobureaucracy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8eae80be88c9775123","definition":"A system of administration based upon organisation into bureaus, division of labour, a hierarchy of authority, etc., designed to dispose of a large body of work in a routine manner.","example":"At that time the administration replaced the system of patronage in the civil service with a bureaucracy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["antibureaucracy","bureaucrap","bureaucrat","bureaucratese","bureaucratic","bureaucratically","bureaucratize","bureaucrazy","bureaupathology","Eurocracy","technobureaucracy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed938b75a2a45dc660","definition":"The body of officers and administrators, especially of a government.","example":"The bureaucracy is expanding to meet the needs of the expanding bureaucracy. (apocryphal quip)","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["antibureaucracy","bureaucrap","bureaucrat","bureaucratese","bureaucratic","bureaucratically","bureaucratize","bureaucrazy","bureaupathology","Eurocracy","technobureaucracy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cec057e0d3f2db0b76","definition":"Excessive red tape and routine in any administration, body or behaviour.","example":"The head of the civil service promised to clamp down on bureaucracy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["papyrocracy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"countable, derogatory, uncountable","wordFamily":["antibureaucracy","bureaucrap","bureaucrat","bureaucratese","bureaucratic","bureaucratically","bureaucratize","bureaucrazy","bureaupathology","Eurocracy","technobureaucracy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/bjʊəˈɹɒk.ɹə.si/"},"wordFamily":["antibureaucracy","bureaucrap","bureaucrat","bureaucratese","bureaucratic","bureaucratically","bureaucratize","bureaucrazy","bureaupathology","Eurocracy","technobureaucracy"]}